Why I Stopped Using PostgreSQL for Side Projects (And You Should Too)
SQLite is faster, simpler, and zero-maintenance. Here's my production setup that handles 10K+ queries/minute on a $5 VPS. For side projects, small SaaS, and solo developer tools: SQLite > PostgreSQL > MySQL Fighting words? Let me show you the numbers. My previous stack for every project: Node.js → PostgreSQL (via pg library) → hosted on Railway/Neon Monthly cost: $5-20 Cold starts: 2-5 seconds Setup time: 30 minutes
My current stack: Node.js → SQLite (via better-sqlite3) → local file Monthly cost: $0 Cold starts: 0 (it's a file) Setup time: 2 minutes
